<title>USA: Tigera sets 1-for-4 reverse stock split.</title>
<headline>Tigera sets 1-for-4 reverse stock split.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tigera Group Inc said its shareholders approved a 1-for-4 reverse stock split and voted to change the company's name to Connectivity Technologies Inc.</p>
<p>The stock split will reduce the number of common shares outstanding to 5.6 million from 22.3 million, it said.</p>
<p>The shares will begin trading on a post-split basis in mid-December, it added.</p>
<p>The new name better describes the company's wire and cable business, Chairman Donald Pascal said in a statement.</p>
</text>
